e-invert dark"><p>The <strong>GET /devices</strong> method in the LG ThinQ =
Connect API retrieves a list of devices registered to the ThinQ server. How=
ever, the API documentation does not mention support for webhooks or push n=
otifications specifically for this method. To stay updated with any changes=
 in the device list, you may need to periodically call the <strong>GET /dev=
ices</strong> method to retrieve the latest information.</p><p>For real-tim=
e notifications about device events, the ThinQ Connect API offers other met=
hods, such as subscribing to push messages from devices. This allows your s=
ervice to receive notifications like "Laundry complete" or "Replace parts" =
when certain events occur on the devices. To implement this functionality, =
you can use the <strong>POST /push/{device-id}</strong> method to subscribe=
 to push notifications for a specific device. <span><span class=3D"" data-s=
tate=3D"closed"><div class=3D"relative inline-flex items-center"><a href=3D=
