e been removed from the user=E2=80=99s account or otherwise de-registered f=
rom the ThinQ platform.</li><li>Your goal is to identify which devices are =
<strong>no longer present</strong> in the new API response and handle them =
appropriately (such as marking them as "inactive" or "deleted").</li></ul><=
h3>Efficiently Identifying Removed Devices</h3><p>You <strong>don=E2=80=99t=
 need to traverse each device=E2=80=99s full data</strong> if you handle th=
is correctly. Here=E2=80=99s how you can approach it efficiently:</p><h4>1.=
 <strong>Use Device IDs to Track Changes</strong></h4><ul><li>When you firs=
t fetch and store the list of devices (e.g., 100 devices), you save their <=
strong>unique device IDs</strong> in your database.</li><li>On the next cal=
l, you get a new list (e.g., 125 devices). Here=E2=80=99s the process:<ul><=
li><strong>Extract the device IDs</strong> from the new list of devices.</l=
i><li>Compare the new set of device IDs with the existing ones in your data=
base.</li></ul></li></ul><h4>2. <strong>Finding Missing Devices</strong></h=
4><ul><li><strong>Devices that are no longer in the new API response</stron=
g> will simply not appear in the new list of device IDs.</li><li>To efficie=
ntly handle this:<ul><li><strong>Query your database</strong> to check whic=
h devices from the previous call (yesterday=E2=80=99s list) do not appear i=
n today=E2=80=99s list.</li><li><strong>For each device</strong> that is mi=
ssing (i.e., not found in the new list of device IDs), mark it as "inactive=
" or "removed" (or just delete it, depending on your use case).</li></ul></=
li></ul><h4>3. <strong>Efficient Comparison</strong></h4><ul><li>This can b=
e done efficiently by storing the <strong>device IDs</strong> in a separate=
 table or as a list in your database (e.g., using sets in some NoSQL databa=
ses or indexed columns in relational databases).</li><li>By using an <stron=
g>index</strong> on the <code>device-id</code> column, your database can qu=
ickly determine which devices have been removed without needing to traverse=
